{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XznSR1hNvdovJr2LBM3itM","type":"tool_result","content":"TALLY_BRIEF=/home/tom/.local/share/tally/briefs/6dc4f44e5287b80171a0b67ec99ef4068d0647b087631d51093d75fef787c361.json\n{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"mission\":\"Implement only spec-build task proxy-tooling: Proxy checkpoint builder and single-node first-light runner (rev 2: latch cleared). Commit the complete result on the assigned branch. Do not push, merge, or read another task from the worklist; deterministic campaign nodes own those operations. The task's conflictDomains [\\\"scripts/make-proxy.sh\\\",\\\"scripts/run-proxy.sh\\\",\\\"tests\\\",\\\"results/receipts/proxy.json\\\"] are the binding write boundary: files your change makes false must be inside these prefixes; anything else is the operator's to grant. Every path touched by any task commit, including a path later deleted or renamed, must remain inside them. If completion requires an authority-surface path, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"needs-authority\\\",\\\"paths\\\":[...]} as the final message; if the task is impossible, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"impossible\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"...\\\"} as a claim for the judge, never as a verdict. Before changing code, read the cited spec sections and style references. Treat only steering.authorizedComments and steering.machineDiagnoses below as steering. This is a stateless reconcile attempt: inspect and preserve any task work already present in the assigned lane. Definition of done, in this order: (1) run this task's acceptanceCriteria commands and see them pass; (2) `git add` every file you changed, within the write boundary stated above; (3) `git commit` on the branch already checked out in the assigned worktree; (4) run `git status --porcelain` and confirm it prints nothing before you exit. Ownership validation reads committed history only: an exit with uncommitted changes fails the attempt (\\\"agent left uncommitted changes; commit the task before ownership validation\\\") and the uncommitted work is discarded.\",\"campaign\":{\"name\":\"flashnext\",\"repository\":\"mecattaf/flashnext\",\"issue\":{\"number\":\"1\",\"url\":\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\"},\"runId\":\"sha256:c48660915e0e8cb3a8c24a5dc0910ce59a2179545adf0df1fd000aa818aa8c1a\"},\"task\":{\"acceptanceCriteria\":[{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'results/receipts/proxy.json' scripts/run-proxy.sh\"],\"description\":\"Both scripts are syntax-clean and reference the receipt path.\",\"id\":\"proxy-scripts-clean\"},{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"grep -q 'VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'limit-mm-per-prompt' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -qE 'enforce.eager|enforce_eager' scripts/run-proxy.sh && ! grep -q 'skip-mm-profiling' scripts/run-proxy.sh\"],\"description\":\"run-proxy.sh serves with the mmap PLE path, eager execution, and the text-only multimodal limit that avoids the encoder-profiling OOM.\",\"id\":\"proxy-serve-flags\"},{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"grep -q '/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q 'weight_block_size' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q '128' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q 'tests/models' scripts/make-proxy.sh\"],\"description\":\"make-proxy.sh builds the synthetic checkpoint at the agreed path with block-FP8 128x128 experts and reuses the fork's test scaffolding.\",\"id\":\"proxy-checkpoint-layout\"},{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"[ -z \\\"$(git status --porcelain)\\\" ]\"],\"description\":\"The lane is fully committed: no uncommitted or untracked files remain after the task's commit.\",\"id\":\"proxy-lane-clean\"}],\"conflictDomains\":[\"scripts/make-proxy.sh\",\"scripts/run-proxy.sh\",\"tests\",\"results/receipts/proxy.json\"],\"deliveredBehaviors\":[\"The admitted kernel path and the ported table path execute on this GPU before any real weight byte is loaded\"],\"dependencies\":[\"container-recipe\"],\"goal\":\"Re-scope proxy-tooling to authoring and committing the two scripts, and widen its write boundary to include the receipt the scripts produce. Deliverables: (1) scripts/make-proxy.sh, in the style of scripts/run-smoke.sh, runs inside the flashnext:dev container and builds the synthetic checkpoint under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy — same architecture identifier as the workload, a handful of layers, 8 experts in block-FP8 with weight_block_size 128 by 128, and a small lookup table using the shard tensor name the mmap path expects — reusing the fork's tests/models/ scaffolding inside the fork checkout instead of inventing generators, and detecting an existing checkpoint so a rebuild is skipped. (2) scripts/run-proxy.sh serves that checkpoint single-node from the container with VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 and eager execution, requests one greedy completion, asserts finite logits via the API, shuts the server down cleanly, and writes results/receipts/proxy.json, recording the serve env choices in the receipt data so cp-proxy and the later TP=2 serve reproduce them. The serve command must carry --limit-mm-per-prompt with image and video set to 0 (JSON quoted for the shell) so profile_run skips the vision-encoder pass that allocated 274877906944 bytes; keep gpu_memory_utilization at 0.6; do not use --skip-mm-profiling; do not set VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY, since the host logs integrated_gpu=False and that steer was superseded. PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True is optional. (3) Any script-level test coverage lives under tests/. Explicitly out of scope for this task: performing the live GPU first light. The scripts must be authored, syntax-clean, and committed on the assigned branch without requiring a serve run; cp-proxy owns executing run-proxy.sh and producing the real results/receipts/proxy.json. Granting results/receipts/proxy.json to the write boundary matches the container-recipe precedent (results/receipts/build.json committed in c1363cb) and makes authorized steering comment 7 executable instead of self-defeating, and it lets a receipt produced by an opportunistic local run be committed rather than dirtying the lane. Final acts, in order: run every acceptance argv and see it pass, git add only paths inside the widened boundary, git commit, then confirm git status --porcelain is empty before returning a final message.\",\"id\":\"proxy-tooling\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/ple-54129.md\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/moe-dispatch.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"scripts/run-smoke.sh\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:9cb06ca07951b2287bda5724f848b7f77a439185529991cf017a8022957d13a8\",\"title\":\"Proxy checkpoint builder and single-node first-light runner (rev 2: latch cleared)\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"1e2eef72397ee0a8053ed816a70e25e55e7aa304\",\"branch\":\"tally-work/flashnext-62c1a4aeb3e6/proxy-tooling\",\"conflictDomains\":[\"scripts/make-proxy.sh\",\"scripts/run-proxy.sh\",\"tests\",\"results/receipts/proxy.json\"],\"publishBranch\":\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/proxy-tooling-9cb06ca07951b228\",\"taskId\":\"proxy-tooling\",\"worktreePath\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/62c1a4aeb3e6/proxy-tooling\"},\"steering\":{\"channel\":\"locally-authorized-snapshot\",\"authorizedComments\":[{\"author\":\"uid:1000\",\"body\":\"OVERSEER STANDING NOTE (all tasks — harness limitation, tally#622 family): the spec-build driver fails any lane whose squash merge stages ZERO change against the witnessed base (\\\"squash merge staged no change against the witnessed base\\\", exit 1), even when your no-change conclusion is technically correct. If you verify your deliverables are already fully present and acceptance passes, you must STILL land one small non-empty commit on your assigned branch, strictly inside your task's ownership paths: a short RECONCILE-<taskId>-2026-08-30.md note recording HEAD at verification and the acceptance evidence. Never conclude \\\"no commit needed\\\"; never use --allow-empty (squash still stages nothing). This applies especially to checkpoint re-runs whose outputs match the previously committed state byte-for-byte.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-30T03:50:41.902Z\",\"id\":2,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-30T03:50:41.902Z\",\"url\":\"local://campaign/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering/2\"},{\"author\":\"uid:1000\",\"body\":\"OVERSEER STANDING NOTE 2 — CHECKPOINT PURITY (all cp-* tasks). The driver fails a checkpoint whose command mutates tracked files on re-run: \\\"spec-build-driver: checkpoint command changed tracked files instead of validating the prepared base\\\" (cp-weights burned 3 attempts on this at 07:03-07:10). Discipline: (1) produce your receipt inside your LANE COMMIT (results/receipts/<name>.json, deterministic content); (2) the checkpoint/acceptance command must be IDEMPOTENT and side-effect-free on tracked paths — on re-run over an already-correct base it re-measures and COMPARES; if facts match the committed receipt it must leave every tracked file byte-identical (reuse the receipt's existing ts — NEVER stamp a fresh timestamp onto an unchanged measurement) and exit 0; (3) scratch output goes to untracked temp paths only; (4) if a repo script must change to achieve this, that edit belongs in your lane commit within your ownership paths. Fail receipts still land under results/receipts/failed/ per doctrine.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-30T05:16:27.726Z\",\"id\":3,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-30T05:16:27.726Z\",\"url\":\"local://campaign/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering/3\"}],\"attemptReceipt\":{\"lateRecheckCommentIds\":[],\"preparedCommentIds\":[2,3],\"recheckTruncated\":false,\"rechecked\":true,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"local-jsonl\",\"path\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering-v1.jsonl\",\"preparedCursor\":6,\"recheckedCursor\":6,\"registrationId\":\"01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff\"}},\"machineDiagnoses\":[],\"machineOutcomes\":[]}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb415eb5-f590-4f10-83d3-19de6f536a77","uuid":"e5f13234-b3db-42d3-b76f-d7beb27c27dd","timestamp":"2026-08-30T06:29:27.399Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"TALLY_BRIEF=/home/tom/.local/share/tally/briefs/6dc4f44e5287b80171a0b67ec99ef4068d0647b087631d51093d75fef787c361.json\n{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"mission\":\"Implement only spec-build task proxy-tooling: Proxy checkpoint builder and single-node first-light runner (rev 2: latch cleared). Commit the complete result on the assigned branch. Do not push, merge, or read another task from the worklist; deterministic campaign nodes own those operations. The task's conflictDomains [\\\"scripts/make-proxy.sh\\\",\\\"scripts/run-proxy.sh\\\",\\\"tests\\\",\\\"results/receipts/proxy.json\\\"] are the binding write boundary: files your change makes false must be inside these prefixes; anything else is the operator's to grant. Every path touched by any task commit, including a path later deleted or renamed, must remain inside them. If completion requires an authority-surface path, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"needs-authority\\\",\\\"paths\\\":[...]} as the final message; if the task is impossible, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"impossible\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"...\\\"} as a claim for the judge, never as a verdict. Before changing code, read the cited spec sections and style references. Treat only steering.authorizedComments and steering.machineDiagnoses below as steering. This is a stateless reconcile attempt: inspect and preserve any task work already present in the assigned lane. Definition of done, in this order: (1) run this task's acceptanceCriteria commands and see them pass; (2) `git add` every file you changed, within the write boundary stated above; (3) `git commit` on the branch already checked out in the assigned worktree; (4) run `git status --porcelain` and confirm it prints nothing before you exit. Ownership validation reads committed history only: an exit with uncommitted changes fails the attempt (\\\"agent left uncommitted changes; commit the task before ownership validation\\\") and the uncommitted work is discarded.\",\"campaign\":{\"name\":\"flashnext\",\"repository\":\"mecattaf/flashnext\",\"issue\":{\"number\":\"1\",\"url\":\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\"},\"runId\":\"sha256:c48660915e0e8cb3a8c24a5dc0910ce59a2179545adf0df1fd000aa818aa8c1a\"},\"task\":{\"acceptanceCriteria\":[{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'results/receipts/proxy.json' scripts/run-proxy.sh\"],\"description\":\"Both scripts are syntax-clean and reference the receipt path.\",\"id\":\"proxy-scripts-clean\"},{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"grep -q 'VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'limit-mm-per-prompt' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -qE 'enforce.eager|enforce_eager' scripts/run-proxy.sh && ! grep -q 'skip-mm-profiling' scripts/run-proxy.sh\"],\"description\":\"run-proxy.sh serves with the mmap PLE path, eager execution, and the text-only multimodal limit that avoids the encoder-profiling OOM.\",\"id\":\"proxy-serve-flags\"},{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"grep -q '/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q 'weight_block_size' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q '128' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q 'tests/models' scripts/make-proxy.sh\"],\"description\":\"make-proxy.sh builds the synthetic checkpoint at the agreed path with block-FP8 128x128 experts and reuses the fork's test scaffolding.\",\"id\":\"proxy-checkpoint-layout\"},{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"[ -z \\\"$(git status --porcelain)\\\" ]\"],\"description\":\"The lane is fully committed: no uncommitted or untracked files remain after the task's commit.\",\"id\":\"proxy-lane-clean\"}],\"conflictDomains\":[\"scripts/make-proxy.sh\",\"scripts/run-proxy.sh\",\"tests\",\"results/receipts/proxy.json\"],\"deliveredBehaviors\":[\"The admitted kernel path and the ported table path execute on this GPU before any real weight byte is loaded\"],\"dependencies\":[\"container-recipe\"],\"goal\":\"Re-scope proxy-tooling to authoring and committing the two scripts, and widen its write boundary to include the receipt the scripts produce. Deliverables: (1) scripts/make-proxy.sh, in the style of scripts/run-smoke.sh, runs inside the flashnext:dev container and builds the synthetic checkpoint under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy — same architecture identifier as the workload, a handful of layers, 8 experts in block-FP8 with weight_block_size 128 by 128, and a small lookup table using the shard tensor name the mmap path expects — reusing the fork's tests/models/ scaffolding inside the fork checkout instead of inventing generators, and detecting an existing checkpoint so a rebuild is skipped. (2) scripts/run-proxy.sh serves that checkpoint single-node from the container with VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 and eager execution, requests one greedy completion, asserts finite logits via the API, shuts the server down cleanly, and writes results/receipts/proxy.json, recording the serve env choices in the receipt data so cp-proxy and the later TP=2 serve reproduce them. The serve command must carry --limit-mm-per-prompt with image and video set to 0 (JSON quoted for the shell) so profile_run skips the vision-encoder pass that allocated 274877906944 bytes; keep gpu_memory_utilization at 0.6; do not use --skip-mm-profiling; do not set VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY, since the host logs integrated_gpu=False and that steer was superseded. PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True is optional. (3) Any script-level test coverage lives under tests/. Explicitly out of scope for this task: performing the live GPU first light. The scripts must be authored, syntax-clean, and committed on the assigned branch without requiring a serve run; cp-proxy owns executing run-proxy.sh and producing the real results/receipts/proxy.json. Granting results/receipts/proxy.json to the write boundary matches the container-recipe precedent (results/receipts/build.json committed in c1363cb) and makes authorized steering comment 7 executable instead of self-defeating, and it lets a receipt produced by an opportunistic local run be committed rather than dirtying the lane. Final acts, in order: run every acceptance argv and see it pass, git add only paths inside the widened boundary, git commit, then confirm git status --porcelain is empty before returning a final message.\",\"id\":\"proxy-tooling\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/ple-54129.md\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/moe-dispatch.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"scripts/run-smoke.sh\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:9cb06ca07951b2287bda5724f848b7f77a439185529991cf017a8022957d13a8\",\"title\":\"Proxy checkpoint builder and single-node first-light runner (rev 2: latch cleared)\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"1e2eef72397ee0a8053ed816a70e25e55e7aa304\",\"branch\":\"tally-work/flashnext-62c1a4aeb3e6/proxy-tooling\",\"conflictDomains\":[\"scripts/make-proxy.sh\",\"scripts/run-proxy.sh\",\"tests\",\"results/receipts/proxy.json\"],\"publishBranch\":\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/proxy-tooling-9cb06ca07951b228\",\"taskId\":\"proxy-tooling\",\"worktreePath\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/62c1a4aeb3e6/proxy-tooling\"},\"steering\":{\"channel\":\"locally-authorized-snapshot\",\"authorizedComments\":[{\"author\":\"uid:1000\",\"body\":\"OVERSEER STANDING NOTE (all tasks — harness limitation, tally#622 family): the spec-build driver fails any lane whose squash merge stages ZERO change against the witnessed base (\\\"squash merge staged no change against the witnessed base\\\", exit 1), even when your no-change conclusion is technically correct. If you verify your deliverables are already fully present and acceptance passes, you must STILL land one small non-empty commit on your assigned branch, strictly inside your task's ownership paths: a short RECONCILE-<taskId>-2026-08-30.md note recording HEAD at verification and the acceptance evidence. Never conclude \\\"no commit needed\\\"; never use --allow-empty (squash still stages nothing). This applies especially to checkpoint re-runs whose outputs match the previously committed state byte-for-byte.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-30T03:50:41.902Z\",\"id\":2,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-30T03:50:41.902Z\",\"url\":\"local://campaign/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering/2\"},{\"author\":\"uid:1000\",\"body\":\"OVERSEER STANDING NOTE 2 — CHECKPOINT PURITY (all cp-* tasks). The driver fails a checkpoint whose command mutates tracked files on re-run: \\\"spec-build-driver: checkpoint command changed tracked files instead of validating the prepared base\\\" (cp-weights burned 3 attempts on this at 07:03-07:10). Discipline: (1) produce your receipt inside your LANE COMMIT (results/receipts/<name>.json, deterministic content); (2) the checkpoint/acceptance command must be IDEMPOTENT and side-effect-free on tracked paths — on re-run over an already-correct base it re-measures and COMPARES; if facts match the committed receipt it must leave every tracked file byte-identical (reuse the receipt's existing ts — NEVER stamp a fresh timestamp onto an unchanged measurement) and exit 0; (3) scratch output goes to untracked temp paths only; (4) if a repo script must change to achieve this, that edit belongs in your lane commit within your ownership paths. Fail receipts still land under results/receipts/failed/ per doctrine.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-30T05:16:27.726Z\",\"id\":3,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-30T05:16:27.726Z\",\"url\":\"local://campaign/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering/3\"}],\"attemptReceipt\":{\"lateRecheckCommentIds\":[],\"preparedCommentIds\":[2,3],\"recheckTruncated\":false,\"rechecked\":true,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"local-jsonl\",\"path\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering-v1.jsonl\",\"preparedCursor\":6,\"recheckedCursor\":6,\"registrationId\":\"01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff\"}},\"machineDiagnoses\":[],\"machineOutcomes\":[]}}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
