ap.py:869-891` (`_attach_table`), with a comment at `ple_mmap.py:866-868` calling them \"two self-consistent halves of the same mapping\". [S] The runtime lookup is `shard = uniq // self.shard_size` (`ple_mmap.py:367`) — pure row arithmetic, no `tp_rank` anywhere. TP sharding in the stock path is an *orthogonal* second split applied by `VocabParallelEmbedding` (`vocab_parallel_embedding.py:313-314`), and `copy_ple_embedding_shard_` is what intersects the two (`nvidia/ple_layer.py:534-540`, `tp_start=/tp_end=` from `shard_indices`). [S]\n155:Nuance on the campaign's phrasing \"FILE shards\": a shard is a *named tensor*, and `discover_shards` does not require one file per shard — it records whichever file holds it. In the test fixture each shard happens to get its own file (`tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_ple_mmap.py:112-124`, `model-ple-{layer_idx}-{shard_index:05d}.safetensors`). [S] So: \"checkpoint row-block tensors, located by file+offset\" is the exact statement; \"not TP shards\" is correct.\n157:Contract test: `test_shard_mapping_matches_upstream_checkpoint_math_at_boundaries`, `tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_ple_mmap.py:369-411`, drives real boundary rows through `MmapPleTable.gather` and compares against the logical table. [S]\n241:# Keep num_reqs-dependent ID generation outside PIECEWISE CUDA graphs,\n262:Call site: `nvidia/ple_layer.py:284`, inside `Qwen4ExpNGramEmbedding.__init__`, i.e. at **construction time, before the ~78 GiB backbone streams** (`ple_mmap.py:703-704` comment [CL]). Tests pin all three: `tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_ple_mmap.py:661`, `:680`, `:691`, `:705`, plus construction-level mirrors at `:758`, `:786`, `:814`. [S]\n306:The mmap path is **FP8-only by construction**: `_FP8_DTYPES` admits only `F8_E4M3` (`ple_mmap.py:78-84`), and `_validate_layer_shards` raises for anything else (`ple_mmap.py:687-693`). Its output is a raw `float8_e4m3fn` tensor (`ple_mmap.py:567-573`), which the nvidia layer dequantizes at `nvidia/ple_layer.py:1194`:\n339:| W3 | **`:281-291`** | the constructor branch — annotation `self.ngram_embedding: VocabParallelEmbedding \\| ple_mmap.MmapNgramEmbedding`; `if ple_mmap.enabled():`; `vllm_config = get_current_vllm_config()`; `ple_mmap.check_cudagraph_safety(vllm_config.compilation_config)`; `ple_mmap.validate_shards_for(vllm_config.model_config, layer_name, self.head_dim)`; `self.ngram_embedding = ple_mmap.MmapNgramEmbedding(padded_vocab_size, self.head_dim)`; `else:` + reindent of `:292-301` |\n342:| W5b | **`:517-527`** (+ `:533`, `:535`, `:538-539`) | `load_weights` shard-drop → `embedding.weights_streamed = True; loaded.add(...); continue`, plus `stock_embedding = cast(VocabParallelEmbedding, embedding)` and the three renamed reads; also the hoist of `embedding = self.ngram_embedding` to `:461` |\n344:The campaign record's citation of **`nvidia/ple_layer.py:281-288` plus a piecewise-cudagraph guard is accurate but incomplete** — it names W3 only (and `:281-288` is 8 of W3's 11 lines; the block ends at `:291` with the `else:`). W4/W5 are equally load-bearing: without W4 the AMD path still calls its own `qwen4_exp_amd_ple_ngram_embedding` op with `dtype=self.ngram_embedding.params_dtype` (`amd/ple_layer.py:315-323`), and `MmapNgramEmbedding` **has no `params_dtype` attribute** (it exposes `torch_dtype`, `ple_mmap.py:535`) — an immediate `AttributeError` on the first forward. Without W5 the loader would materialize the full table into a placeholder that has no `.weight`, raising in `copy_ple_embedding_shard_`.\n354:1. `from . import ple_mmap` — but `ple_mmap.py` lives in `nvidia/`. Two options: **(a)** `from ..nvidia import ple_mmap` in both `amd/ple_layer.py` and `amd/model.py` — safe, because `nvidia/__init__.py` is an SPDX-only stub (3 lines, no re-exports) [S], so this pulls in *only* `ple_mmap.py` and none of the CUDA-heavy nvidia modules; **(b)** relocate to `vllm/models/qwen4_exp/common/ple_mmap.py` alongside `common/ple.py` and update both trees + all `tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_ple_mmap.py` imports (the test file imports `vllm.models.qwen4_exp.nvidia.ple_mmap` at `:27` and `vllm.models.qwen4_exp.nvidia.model` at `:26`). (b) is the cleaner upstream shape; (a) is the smaller diff.\n358:5. Guards: `check_cudagraph_safety` + `validate_shards_for`, both at construction (`nvidia/ple_layer.py:284-287`), unchanged — no AMD variant.\n367:- Plus, if option (b), a file move and a test-import sweep across 2048 lines of `tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_ple_mmap.py`, which is nvidia-only today: `grep -cni 'amd\\|rocm' tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_ple_mmap.py` → `0`. [M]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
