{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YHZV1CcV1TrjrbywRa29r8","type":"tool_result","content":"45:def __getattr__(name: str) -> Any:\n98:`MmapNgramEmbedding` is declared `class MmapNgramEmbedding(nn.Module)` at `nvidia/ple_mmap.py:506` [S] and constructed with the **full padded vocab**: `ple_mmap.MmapNgramEmbedding(padded_vocab_size, self.head_dim)` at `nvidia/ple_layer.py:288-290` [S] — the identical `padded_vocab_size` handed to the vocab-parallel constructor in the `else:` branch at `:292-293`.\n153:**`shard_0` / `shard_1` are NOT TP shards. Confirmed.** [S] Precisely: `shard_i` is the *i*-th **row block of the logical table as stored under its own checkpoint tensor name**, produced by the checkpoint's `split_ngram_parts` split (default 512, `nvidia/ple_layer.py:241`). The mapping is `shard_size = (org_vocab_size + split_ngram_parts - 1) // split_ngram_parts; checkpoint_start = shard_index * shard_size` — written twice, verbatim, at `nvidia/ple_layer.py:502-509` (loader) and `ple_mmap.py:869-891` (`_attach_table`), with a comment at `ple_mmap.py:866-868` calling them \"two self-consistent halves of the same mapping\". [S] The runtime lookup is `shard = uniq // self.shard_size` (`ple_mmap.py:367`) — pure row arithmetic, no `tp_rank` anywhere. TP sharding in the stock path is an *orthogonal* second split applied by `VocabParallelEmbedding` (`vocab_parallel_embedding.py:313-314`), and `copy_ple_embedding_shard_` is what intersects the two (`nvidia/ple_layer.py:534-540`, `tp_start=/tp_end=` from `shard_indices`). [S]\n155:Nuance on the campaign's phrasing \"FILE shards\": a shard is a *named tensor*, and `discover_shards` does not require one file per shard — it records whichever file holds it. In the test fixture each shard happens to get its own file (`tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_ple_mmap.py:112-124`, `model-ple-{layer_idx}-{shard_index:05d}.safetensors`). [S] So: \"checkpoint row-block tensors, located by file+offset\" is the exact statement; \"not TP shards\" is correct.\n157:Contract test: `test_shard_mapping_matches_upstream_checkpoint_math_at_boundaries`, `tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_ple_mmap.py:369-411`, drives real boundary rows through `MmapPleTable.gather` and compares against the logical table. [S]\n231:| `nvidia/model.py` | +14/−12 [M] | 12 of those are upstream drift (as above); the mmap wiring is `from vllm.config import VllmConfig, get_current_vllm_config` (`:12`), `from . import ple_mmap` (`:77`), and two 5-line `build_tables` blocks at `:812-817` and `:1011-1016`. [S] |\n235:`#54129`'s head is literally a merge of `upstream-main` into `ple-mmap-upstream`, and its non-PLE churn (fused-MoE oracle, quark OCP MX, flashinfer utils, kimi_k3) is that merge. `#53896` never had `ple_mmap.py` (`grep -c PLE_MMAP vllm-pr53896/vllm/envs.py` → `0`; `find vllm-pr53896 -name 'ple_mmap*' -o -name 'test_ple_mmap*' | wc -l` → `0`) [M]. So the mmap feature is strictly additive on top of #53896's model code, but the two branches have **already diverged on shared non-mmap files** and a merge will conflict on `amd/{model,mtp}.py`, `nvidia/{model,mtp}.py`, `vllm/config/compilation.py`, and `vllm/envs.py`.\n262:Call site: `nvidia/ple_layer.py:284`, inside `Qwen4ExpNGramEmbedding.__init__`, i.e. at **construction time, before the ~78 GiB backbone streams** (`ple_mmap.py:703-704` comment [CL]). Tests pin all three: `tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_ple_mmap.py:661`, `:680`, `:691`, `:705`, plus construction-level mirrors at `:758`, `:786`, `:814`. [S]\n287:| `VLLM_PLE_MMAP` | `False` (`\"0\"`) | `bool(int(os.getenv(...)))` | Master gate. `ple_mmap.enabled()` (`ple_mmap.py:116-118`) returns it; drives the constructor swap (`nvidia/ple_layer.py:282`), the three guards, the `load_weights` interception, and `build_tables` (`nvidia/model.py:813`, `:1012`). | `envs.py:325`, `:2170` |\n339:| W3 | **`:281-291`** | the constructor branch — annotation `self.ngram_embedding: VocabParallelEmbedding \\| ple_mmap.MmapNgramEmbedding`; `if ple_mmap.enabled():`; `vllm_config = get_current_vllm_config()`; `ple_mmap.check_cudagraph_safety(vllm_config.compilation_config)`; `ple_mmap.validate_shards_for(vllm_config.model_config, layer_name, self.head_dim)`; `self.ngram_embedding = ple_mmap.MmapNgramEmbedding(padded_vocab_size, self.head_dim)`; `else:` + reindent of `:292-301` |\n349:- `:812-817` and `:1011-1016` — after `loader.load_weights(...)`: `if ple_mmap.enabled(): ple_mmap.build_tables(self.model_config, get_current_vllm_config().compilation_config)`; `return loaded`\n354:1. `from . import ple_mmap` — but `ple_mmap.py` lives in `nvidia/`. Two options: **(a)** `from ..nvidia import ple_mmap` in both `amd/ple_layer.py` and `amd/model.py` — safe, because `nvidia/__init__.py` is an SPDX-only stub (3 lines, no re-exports) [S], so this pulls in *only* `ple_mmap.py` and none of the CUDA-heavy nvidia modules; **(b)** relocate to `vllm/models/qwen4_exp/common/ple_mmap.py` alongside `common/ple.py` and update both trees + all `tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_ple_mmap.py` imports (the test file imports `vllm.models.qwen4_exp.nvidia.ple_mmap` at `:27` and `vllm.models.qwen4_exp.nvidia.model` at `:26`). (b) is the cleaner upstream shape; (a) is the smaller diff.\n367:- Plus, if option (b), a file move and a test-import sweep across 2048 lines of `tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_ple_mmap.py`, which is nvidia-only today: `grep -cni 'amd\\|rocm' tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_ple_mmap.py` → `0`. [M]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb415eb5-f590-4f10-83d3-19de6f536a77","uuid":"e4c083b6-bfc3-49e3-b150-b91bc7ccbacf","timestamp":"2026-08-30T06:30:19.177Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"45:def __getattr__(name: str) -> Any:\n98:`MmapNgramEmbedding` is declared `class MmapNgramEmbedding(nn.Module)` at `nvidia/ple_mmap.py:506` [S] and constructed with the **full padded vocab**: `ple_mmap.MmapNgramEmbedding(padded_vocab_size, self.head_dim)` at `nvidia/ple_layer.py:288-290` [S] — the iden