{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014k8b5Fvsd5rCuTFJmQpAaz","type":"tool_result","content":"Its `forward` (`ple_mmap.py:545-573`) contains **no collective, no mask, no rank arithmetic**:\n```\n$ grep -n 'rank\\|tp_\\|world_size\\|parallel\\|all_reduce\\|distributed' vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ple_mmap.py\n(no output; exit 1)\n```\n[M] — zero hits across the whole 1010-line file.\n\n`MmapPleTable.__init__` memory-maps **every** shard with no rank filter: `ple_mmap.py:330-334` [S]:\n```python\nfor idx, (path, offset, rows) in shards.items():\n    self.mm[idx] = np.memmap(path, dtype=np.uint8, mode=\"r\", offset=offset, shape=(rows, row_bytes))\n    self.rows_total += rows\n```\nand `_attach_table` *requires* all expected shards present per rank (`ple_mmap.py:870-878`, `missing = [...]` → `RuntimeError`). [S]\n\n**Verdict**: switching to the mmap path removes the per-token all-reduce/all-gather at the PLE lookup site entirely. The trade is that every rank independently gathers the full-width rows for every token — TP-redundant I/O and TP-redundant host→device copies, in exchange for zero NCCL/RCCL traffic at that site. (The redundancy hits page cache, shared per host, so the *disk* cost is not multiplied — that last clause is my inference from `mode=\"r\"` shared file mappings, not read from source; treat as reasoning, not evidence.)\n\n---\n\n## 3. `load_weights` under `VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1`\n\nThe interception lives in `Qwen4ExpNGramEmbedding.load_weights`, `nvidia/ple_layer.py:450-547`. Two mmap-specific branches:\n\n**(a) weight_scale kept** — `nvidia/ple_layer.py:477-490` [S]:\n```python\nif (isinstance(embedding, ple_mmap.MmapNgramEmbedding)\n        and name == \"ngram_embedding.weight_scale\"):\n    ple_mmap.set_weight_scale(embedding, loaded_weight,\n                              cast(torch.Tensor, self.layer_multipliers).device)\n    loaded.add(name); continue\n```\n`set_weight_scale` registers a non-persistent buffer, `ple_mmap.py:587-590`. [S]\n\n**(b) shard tensors dropped on the floor** — `nvidia/ple_layer.py:517-527` [S]:\n```python\nif isinstance(embedding, ple_mmap.MmapNgramEmbedding):\n    # Served from disk via mmap; the loader still streams\n    # this shard transiently, but it is never retained.\n    embedding.weights_streamed = True\n    loaded.add(\"ngram_embedding.weight\")\n    continue\n```\n`loaded_weight` is never copied anywhere; the reference dies at loop iteration end. **Confirmed: never materialized into a resident table.** Note the honest caveat in the PR's own comment: the *loader* still streams each shard into host memory transiently — the flag removes the resident copy, not the streaming transient. [S]\n\nThe stock (env-off) path immediately below at `:533-541` is the only code that would touch `.weight`/`.shard_indices`; `MmapNgramEmbedding` deliberately has neither (`ple_mmap.py:507-511` docstring). [S]\n\n**Shard discovery.** `discover_shards(model_path)` — `ple_mmap.py:183-268`, `@functools.cache` at `:183`. [S]\n- Globs `os.path.join(model_path, \"*.safetensors\")` (`:209`) and parses each file's header (`:210`, `parse_safetensors_header` at `:125-170`).\n- Matches tensor **names** with `_SHARD_RE = re.compile(r\"layers\\.(\\d+)\\.ple\\.ple_embedding\\.ngram_embedding\\.shard_(\\d+)\\.weight$\")`, `ple_mmap.py:94-96`. [S]\n- Records `per_layer[layer_idx][shard_idx] = (path, data_start + start, rows)` (`:243-247`) — i.e. **(file path, absolute byte offset, row count)**.\n- Header-only reads; the docstring at `:186-191` says \"never the multi-GiB tensor data\". [S/CL]\n- No `model.safetensors.index.json` exists for this checkpoint, hence direct header parsing — `ple_mmap.py:122-123`. [CL — comment]\n\n**`shard_0` / `shard_1` are NOT TP shards. Confirmed.** [S] Precisely: `shard_i` is the *i*-th **row block of the logical table as stored under its own checkpoint tensor name**, produced by the checkpoint's `split_ngram_parts` split (default 512, `nvidia/ple_layer.py:241`). The mapping is `shard_size = (org_vocab_size + split_ngram_parts - 1) // split_ngram_parts; checkpoint_start = shard_index * shard_size` — written twice, verbatim, at `nvidia/ple_layer.py:502-509` (loader) and `ple_mmap.py:869-891` (`_attach_table`), with a comment at `ple_mmap.py:866-868` calling them \"two self-consistent halves of the same mapping\". [S] The runtime lookup is `shard = uniq // self.shard_size` (`ple_mmap.py:367`) — pure row arithmetic, no `tp_rank` anywhere. TP sharding in the stock path is an *orthogonal* second split applied by `VocabParallelEmbedding` (`vocab_parallel_embedding.py:313-314`), and `copy_ple_embedding_shard_` is what intersects the two (`nvidia/ple_layer.py:534-540`, `tp_start=/tp_end=` from `shard_indices`). [S]\n\nNuance on the campaign's phrasing \"FILE shards\": a shard is a *named tensor*, and `discover_shards` does not require one file per shard — it records whichever file holds it. In the test fixture each shard happens to get its own file (`tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_ple_mmap.py:112-124`, `model-ple-{layer_idx}-{shard_index:05d}.safetensors`). [S] So: \"checkpoint row-block tensors, located by file+offset\" is the exact statement; \"not TP shards\" is correct.\n\nContract test: `test_shard_mapping_matches_upstream_checkpoint_math_at_boundaries`, `tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_ple_mmap.py:369-411`, drives real boundary rows through `MmapPleTable.gather` and compares against the logical table. [S]\n\n---\n\n## 4. Memory/staging behavior relevant to UMA (line numbers at THIS head)\n\nAll in `vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ple_mmap.py`:\n\n| Property | Line(s) | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| `np.memmap(..., mode=\"r\", offset=offset, shape=(rows, row_bytes))` | **331-333** | [S] read-only shared mapping, `dtype=np.uint8` |\n| Dedup via `np.unique(..., return_inverse=True)` | **360** | [S] `uniq, inverse = np.unique(ids, return_inverse=True)` |\n| Re-expansion to input order | **405** | [S] `gathered = out[inverse]` |\n| `ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=self.workers)` | **335** | [S] |\n| Chunked tasks, `VLLM_PLE_MMAP_CHUNK` rows each | **377-378** | [S] `for c in range(s, e, self.chunk): tasks.append((si, c, min(c + self.chunk, e)))` |\n| Fan-out over the pool | **391-395** | [S] single task runs inline; else `self.pool.map(run, tasks)` |\n| Fancy-index gather off the memmap (page faults do the I/O; GIL released) | **387** + comment **385-386** | [S/CL] `out[a:b] = mm[local[a:b]]` |\n| **Staging buffer is pageable, not pinned** | **369** | [S] `out = np.empty((uniq.size, self.row_bytes), dtype=np.uint8)` — plain NumPy heap alloc; `torch.from_numpy(rows)` at **567** wraps it |\n| Explicitly stated non-pinned | **568-571** | [CL — comment] \"`rows` … is pageable host memory, not pinned, so this H2D copy is effectively synchronous. Pinned staging (Phase-4 lever 5) is a separate, not-yet-pulled lever\" |\n| H2D copy | **572** | [S] `out = out.to(ids.device, non_blocking=True)` — no-op non-blocking per the comment above |\n| **Device→host sync of the ids, every call** | **558** | [S] `ids_np = ids.detach().to(\"cpu\", non_blocking=False).numpy().reshape(-1)` — an explicit blocking D2H per PLE layer per forward |\n| Prewarm streams via `open(..., buffering=0)` in 64 MiB blocks | **442**, **456-465** | [S] `block = 64 << 20` |\n| Prewarm bound = `min(table_bytes, max(0, MemAvailable - 8 GiB))` | **91**, **493-500** | [S] `_PREWARM_HEADROOM_BYTES = 8 << 30` |\n| `MemAvailable` read from `/proc/meminfo` | **484-490** | [S] |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb415eb5-f590-4f10-83d3-19de6f536a77","uuid":"a3613862-e573-42a9-8b06-62861fdcd376","timestamp":"2026-08-30T06:31:13.731Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Its `forward` (`ple_mmap.py:545-573`) contains **no collective, no mask, no rank arithmetic**:\n```\n$ grep -n 'rank\\|tp_\\|world_size\\|parallel\\|all_reduce\\|distributed' vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ple_mmap.py\n(no output; exit 1)\n```\n[M] — zero hi