{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XTUQH4Bm4BtiwiThDwV7CG","type":"tool_result","content":"ANNOUNCE.md\nCONTINGENCY-sampler-cu-remaining-1024-launches.patch\nDAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md\nDECISIONS-2026-08-30.md\nGATE0.md\nMORNING.md\nUSB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md\n===\ndocs/MORNING.md:78:| `results/receipts/proxy.json` | `scripts/run-proxy.sh` (cp-proxy) | shape only | Claim 4.1: the synthetic checkpoint served single-node with the mmap path engaged, finite output, clean shutdown. `data` records the serve env choices the TP=2 serve then reproduces. |\ndocs/MORNING.md:184:| **UNKNOWN-1** — is the fused-mixture block-FP8 kernel numerically sound on this GPU once admitted? | claims 4.1, 4.4 | Open at render. Read `proxy.json` (finite output) then `fidelity.json` (reference losses, frontier logits). Both green ⇒ drained. |\ndocs/MORNING.md:187:| **UNKNOWN-4** — the fork's runtime behavior on the ruling P4 wheel set | claims 3.1, 4.1 | **Half drained.** `build.json` is banked pass. Runtime half waits on `proxy.json`. |\ndocs/MORNING.md:403:| **The ncclNet-plugin route for the stream primitive** | Rejected **for the latency goal**: it sits under the collective library's proxy/protocol stack, which eats most of the win; HopID scarcity forces a multiplexer over one or two long-lived streams; and comm teardown on every serve restart is exactly the open/close pattern the wedge hazard forbids. 3–5 attended days to a fragile prototype. The doorbell-allreduce port (item 6) is the real path. |\ndocs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md:55:  (`42ae5cd`), L16 test exemption for the agent block, proxy-tooling\ndocs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md:57:  results/receipts/proxy.json, GPU first-light moved to cp-proxy).\ndocs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md:61:Lanes: proxy-tooling (author+commit two scripts — re-scoped, cheap),\ndocs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md:63:Checkpoints: cp-smoke → cp-proxy → cp-tp2 → cp-bench → cp-close.\ndocs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md:68:   EVERY serve (proxy and TP=2). The vision encoder profiling pass\ndocs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md:79:   VLLM_COMPILE/PIECEWISE — the mode the successful proxy boot used). Add\ndocs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md:55:   *above* the library entirely. A net plugin sits *under* its proxy and\ndocs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md:56:   protocol machinery — LL/Simple protocols, host staging, proxy-thread hops —\ndocs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md:76:under the proxy threads, collective hang debugging, p99 validation and\ndocs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md:201:> under the library's proxy/protocol stack (which eats the latency win),\nREADME.md:83:- [ ] proxy-tooling (author the proxy build/serve scripts; cp-proxy executes)\nREADME.md:88:- [ ] cp-smoke → cp-proxy → **cp-tp2 (the milestone)** → cp-bench (MTP spec-on arm) → cp-close\nREADME.md:231:  under the collective library's proxy/protocol stack (which would eat most\nREADME.md:332:dependency-free doc lanes (proxy-tooling, morning-ledger, catalog-handoff,\nREADME.md:335:re-stage (~2.5–3 h), cp-build (banked, skipped), cp-smoke, cp-proxy,\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:207:        \"A client whose prefill number is a measurement, not a proxy\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:237:      \"id\": \"proxy-tooling\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:240:      \"goal\": \"Re-scope proxy-tooling to authoring and committing the two scripts, and widen its write boundary to include the receipt the scripts produce. Deliverables: (1) scripts/make-proxy.sh, in the style of scripts/run-smoke.sh, runs inside the flashnext:dev container and builds the synthetic checkpoint under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy — same architecture identifier as the workload, a handful of layers, 8 experts in block-FP8 with weight_block_size 128 by 128, and a small lookup table using the shard tensor name the mmap path expects — reusing the fork's tests/models/ scaffolding inside the fork checkout instead of inventing generators, and detecting an existing checkpoint so a rebuild is skipped. (2) scripts/run-proxy.sh serves that checkpoint single-node from the container with VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 and eager execution, requests one greedy completion, asserts finite logits via the API, shuts the server down cleanly, and writes results/receipts/proxy.json, recording the serve env choices in the receipt data so cp-proxy and the later TP=2 serve reproduce them. The serve command must carry --limit-mm-per-prompt with image and video set to 0 (JSON quoted for the shell) so profile_run skips the vision-encoder pass that allocated 274877906944 bytes; keep gpu_memory_utilization at 0.6; do not use --skip-mm-profiling; do not set VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY, since the host logs integrated_gpu=False and that steer was superseded. PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True is optional. (3) Any script-level test coverage lives under tests/. Explicitly out of scope for this task: performing the live GPU first light. The scripts must be authored, syntax-clean, and committed on the assigned branch without requiring a serve run; cp-proxy owns executing run-proxy.sh and producing the real results/receipts/proxy.json. Granting results/receipts/proxy.json to the write boundary matches the container-recipe precedent (results/receipts/build.json committed in c1363cb) and makes authorized steering comment 7 executable instead of self-defeating, and it lets a receipt produced by an opportunistic local run be committed rather than dirtying the lane. Final acts, in order: run every acceptance argv and see it pass, git add only paths inside the widened boundary, git commit, then confirm git status --porcelain is empty before returning a final message.\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:256:          \"id\": \"proxy-scripts-clean\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:261:            \"bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'results/receipts/proxy.json' scripts/run-proxy.sh\"\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:265:          \"id\": \"proxy-serve-flags\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:266:          \"description\": \"run-proxy.sh serves with the mmap PLE path, eager execution, and the text-only multimodal limit that avoids the encoder-profiling OOM.\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:270:            \"grep -q 'VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'limit-mm-per-prompt' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -qE 'enforce.eager|enforce_eager' scripts/run-proxy.sh && ! grep -q 'skip-mm-profiling' scripts/run-proxy.sh\"\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:274:          \"id\": \"proxy-checkpoint-layout\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:275:          \"description\": \"make-proxy.sh builds the synthetic checkpoint at the agreed path with block-FP8 128x128 experts and reuses the fork's test scaffolding.\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:279:            \"grep -q '/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q 'weight_block_size' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q '128' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q 'tests/models' scripts/make-proxy.sh\"\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:283:          \"id\": \"proxy-lane-clean\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:296:        \"scripts/make-proxy.sh\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:297:        \"scripts/run-proxy.sh\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:299:        \"results/receipts/proxy.json\"\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:306:      \"goal\": \"AMENDED 2026-08-30: docs/MORNING.md currently holds the operator's 2026-08-29 day-run stop-state record — FIRST move that file verbatim to docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md (git mv, keep every byte), THEN write the new docs/MORNING.md per spec claim 7.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r7). This lane renders BEFORE the milestone checkpoints run (it sits early in the serial graph), so the receipt review table has two row kinds: receipts already banked at render time (build, weights, possibly smoke) carry their observed status and the bound they were graded against; every receipt that lands AFTER render is PRE-DECLARED — one row each for preflight, proxy, tp2, residency, fidelity, context, bench, and usb4stream, naming the file path, the bound scripts/receipts-verify.py grades it against, and how to read it. Three pre-declared rows are mandatory and specific: (a) results/receipts/usb4stream.json — cp-usb4stream runs dead-last after cp-close and only when the pair serve is already down; name its three typed outcomes (ok / skipped:REASON / aborted:PHASE:ERRNO), say that data.outcome is where to read them, that 'skipped:serve-up-on-shared-cable' is the EXPECTED outcome after a healthy night, and that a skipped or aborted outcome is the typed blocker for that step per F.12; (b) results/receipts/failed/ — the quarantine directory: any step that fails its own grading writes its fail receipt THERE so one graded failure cannot redden every later gate run; every file present there in the morning is a typed blocker the operator reviews first; (c) results/receipts/failed/context.json — if present, the honest full-context decode ratio undershot the 0.9 bound (12 full-attention layers walking 256K KV; the community precedent shows about a 2x falloff by 50-73k) — a typed performance finding routed to the optimization menu, deliberately NOT a campaign failure. Also render: the open-items list (every UNKNOWN from the spec with its drain state); the promotion checklist (what the operator verifies before any fleet change, per ruling P13 — and state the causality plainly: the fleet's local-models sync retires any staged artifact that has no catalog row; it pruned the staged checkpoint from BOTH nodes on 08-29 around 20:07/20:14; applying handoff/catalog-row.patch is the act that makes staging durable, and it must precede any rebuild or any restart of the model-sync trigger service); the transport-rung caveat (if any receipt records fn_transport_rung wire-fallback, the night ran on the 5GbE wire: valid but degraded receipts, and bench.json then does NOT satisfy the rail-sockets Gate 0 for verbs bring-up — healing rail 0 is the morning's first transport act); the optimization menu; and a blocker template implementing ruling P16. The optimization menu carries, beyond the original items (tuned mixture-kernel config generation for this GPU, graph-capture matrix, jumbo-frame A-B, draft-length sweep, the four-bit expert lane pointers from IMPORTS.md): the speculative-head depth sweep n in 1 to 4 plus the index-share and padded-drafter knobs (UNKNOWN-5); the attended RDMA go/no-go with the honest cost (2-4 attended hours, two more reboots, worker deploy-path fix first, nothing staged for kernel 7.2.2 yet) and honest expectation (about +3.4 percent measured precedent over held TCP); the stream-primitive morning decision rule (attended port of the reference doorbell allreduce onto the in-tree stream device ONLY if the banked exchange p50 at 8-16 KiB is at or under about 40 microseconds AND the bench matrix shows decode is allreduce-dominated — noting the stream bench likely runs attended in the morning after teardown, since it skips while the pair serves); the full-context decode probe follow-up when deferred; a rejected-with-reason register so nothing is re-litigated (the community int4-WMMA expert lane: bound to a different runtime's artifact, single-device only, unreachable even in its own public release; the indexer rotation plus FP4 QAT art: fidelity art for a different model family's trained indexer graph — our engine's indexer is weight-free bf16 with no such trained graph, so transplanting it would corrupt top-k selection); the load-phase page-cache drop-behind remedy pointer for repo issue 2 (release file pages in chunks behind the loader); a per-shape kernel block-size tuning item for the 2560x640 and 640x2560 expert shapes (community precedent: a forced tile choice beat the auto-selector on exactly these shapes); and a note to audit the drafter hidden-state versus prefix-cache position sync before the speculative profile is declared production (a community v1.1 fix records the failure mode: cached target prefix reused while the drafter state timeline sits elsewhere breaks multi-turn — the operator files the repo issue). Also write docs/ANNOUNCE.md: a short community post draft describing the setup (two 128 GB unified-memory desktops, two fast rails, one control wire), what was built overnight, where the evidence lives, and where benchmarks land. Boundaries: touch only docs/MORNING.md, docs/ANNOUNCE.md, and docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md.\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:471:      \"id\": \"cp-proxy\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:473:      \"title\": \"Checkpoint: proxy checkpoint first light, single node\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:477:        \"bash scripts/make-proxy.sh && bash scripts/run-proxy.sh\"\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:482:        \"proxy-tooling\"\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:495:        \"cp-proxy\",","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb415eb5-f590-4f10-83d3-19de6f536a77","uuid":"b81b6dcc-3e9b-4e67-9e5b-15675aacd6c9","timestamp":"2026-08-30T06:32:19.396Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"ANNOUNCE.md\nCONTINGENCY-sampler-cu-remaining-1024-launches.patch\nDAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md\nDECISIONS-2026-08-30.md\nGATE0.md\nMORNING.md\nUSB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md\n===\ndocs/MORNING.md:78:| `results/receipts/proxy.json` | `scripts/run-proxy.sh` (cp-proxy) | shape only | Claim 4.1: the synthetic checkpoint served single-node with the mmap path engaged, finite output, clean shutdown. `data` records the serve env choices the TP=2 serve then reproduces. |\ndocs/MORNING.md:184:| **UNKNOWN-1** — is the fused-mixture block-FP8 kernel numerically sound on this GPU once admitted? | claims 4.1, 4.4 | Open at render. Read `proxy.json` (finite output) then `fidelity.json` (reference losses, frontier logits). Both green ⇒ drained. |\ndocs/MORNING.md:187:| **UNKNOWN-4** — the fork's runtime behavior on the ruling P4 wheel set | claims 3.1, 4.1 | **Half drained.** `build.json` is banked pass. Runtime half waits on `proxy.json`. |\ndocs/MORNING.md:403:| **The ncclNet-plugin route for the stream primitive** | Rejected **for the latency goal**: it sits under the collective library's proxy/protocol stack, which eats most of the win; HopID scarcity forces a multiplexer over one or two long-lived streams; and comm teardown on every serve restart is exactly the open/close pattern the wedge hazard forbids. 3–5 attended days to a fragile prototype. The doorbell-allreduce port (item 6) is the real path. |\ndocs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md:55:  (`42ae5cd`), L16 test exemption for the agent block, proxy-tooling\ndocs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md:57:  results/receipts/proxy.json, GPU first-light moved to cp-proxy).\ndocs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md:61:Lanes: proxy-tooling (author+commit two scripts — re-scoped, cheap),\ndocs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md:63:Checkpoints: cp-smoke → cp-proxy → cp-tp2 → cp-bench → cp-close.\ndocs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md:68:   EVERY serve (proxy and TP=2). The vision encoder profiling pass\ndocs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md:79:   VLLM_COMPILE/PIECEWISE — the mode the successful proxy boot used). Add\ndocs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md:55:   *above* the library entirely. A net plugin sits *under* its proxy and\ndocs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md:56:   protocol machinery — LL/Simple protocols, host staging, proxy-thread hops —\ndocs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md:76:under the proxy threads, collective hang debugging, p99 validation and\ndocs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md:201:> under the library's proxy/protocol stack (which eats the latency win),\nREADME.md:83:- [ ] proxy-tooling (author the proxy build/serve scripts; cp-proxy executes)\nREADME.md:88:- [ ] cp-smoke → cp-proxy → **cp-tp2 (the milestone)** → cp-bench (MTP spec-on arm) → cp-close\nREADME.md:231:  under the collective library's proxy/protocol stack (which would eat most\nREADME.md:332:dependency-free doc lanes (proxy-tooling, morning-ledger, catalog-handoff,\nREADME.md:335:re-stage (~2.5–3 h), cp-build (banked, skipped), cp-smoke, cp-proxy,\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:207:        \"A client whose prefill number is a measurement, not a proxy\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:237:      \"id\": \"proxy-tooling\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:240:      \"goal\": \"Re-scope proxy-tooling to authoring and committing the two scripts, and widen its write boundary to include the receipt the scripts produce. Deliverables: (1) scripts/make-proxy.sh, in the style of scripts/run-smoke.sh, runs inside the flashnext:dev container and builds the synthetic checkpoint under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy — same architecture identifier as the workload, a handful of layers, 8 experts in block-FP8 with weight_block_size 128 by 128, and a small lookup table using the shard tensor name the mmap path expects — reusing the fork's tests/models/ scaffolding inside the fork checkout instead of inventing generators, and detecting an existing checkpoint so a rebuild is skipped. (2) scripts/run-proxy.sh serves that checkpoint single-node from the container with VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 and eager execution, requests one greedy completion, asserts finite logits via the API, shuts the server down cleanly, and writes results/receipts/proxy.json, recording the serve env choices in the receipt data so cp-proxy and the later TP=2 serve reproduce them. The serve command must carry --limit-mm-per-prompt with image and video set to 0 (JSON quoted for the shell) so profile_run skips the vision-encoder pass that allocated 274877906944 bytes; keep gpu_memory_utilization at 0.6; do not use --skip-mm-profiling; do not set VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY, since the host logs integrated_gpu=False and that steer was superseded. PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True is optional. (3) Any script-level test coverage lives under tests/. Explicitly out of scope for this task: performing the live GPU first light. The scripts must be authored, syntax-clean, and committed on the assigned branch without requiring a serve run; cp-proxy owns executing run-proxy.sh and producing the real results/receipts/proxy.json. Granting results/receipts/proxy.json to the write boundary matches the container-recipe precedent (results/receipts/build.json committed in c1363cb) and makes authorized steering comment 7 executable instead of self-defeating, and it lets a receipt produced by an opportunistic local run be committed rather than dirtying the lane. Final acts, in order: run every acceptance argv and see it pass, git add only paths inside the widened boundary, git commit, then confirm git status --porcelain is empty before returning a final message.\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:256:          \"id\": \"proxy-scripts-clean\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:261:            \"bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'results/receipts/proxy.json' scripts/run-proxy.sh\"\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:265:          \"id\": \"proxy-serve-flags\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:266:          \"description\": \"run-proxy.sh serves with the mmap PLE path, eager execution, and the text-only multimodal limit that avoids the encoder-profiling OOM.\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:270:            \"grep -q 'VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'limit-mm-per-prompt' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -qE 'enforce.eager|enforce_eager' scripts/run-proxy.sh && ! grep -q 'skip-mm-profiling' scripts/run-proxy.sh\"\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:274:          \"id\": \"proxy-checkpoint-layout\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:275:          \"description\": \"make-proxy.sh builds the synthetic checkpoint at the agreed path with block-FP8 128x128 experts and reuses the fork's test scaffolding.\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:279:            \"grep -q '/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q 'weight_block_size' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q '128' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q 'tests/models' scripts/make-proxy.sh\"\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:283:          \"id\": \"proxy-lane-clean\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:296:        \"scripts/make-proxy.sh\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:297:        \"scripts/run-proxy.sh\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:299:        \"results/receipts/proxy.json\"\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:306:      \"goal\": \"AMENDED 2026-08-30: docs/MORNING.md currently holds the operator's 2026-08-29 day-run stop-state record — FIRST move that file verbatim to docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md (git mv, keep every byte), THEN write the new docs/MORNING.md per spec claim 7.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r7). This lane renders BEFORE the milestone checkpoints run (it sits early in the serial graph), so the receipt review table has two row kinds: receipts already banked at render time (build, weights, possibly smoke) carry their observed status and the bound they were graded against; every receipt that lands AFTER render is PRE-DECLARED — one row each for preflight, proxy, tp2, residency, fidelity, context, bench, and usb4stream, naming the file path, the bound scripts/receipts-verify.py grades it against, and how to read it. Three pre-declared rows are mandatory and specific: (a) results/receipts/usb4stream.json — cp-usb4stream runs dead-last after cp-close and only when the pair serve is already down; name its three typed outcomes (ok / skipped:REASON / aborted:PHASE:ERRNO), say that data.outcome is where to read them, that 'skipped:serve-up-on-shared-cable' is the EXPECTED outcome after a healthy night, and that a skipped or aborted outcome is the typed blocker for that step per F.12; (b) results/receipts/failed/ — the quarantine directory: any step that fails its own grading writes its fail receipt THERE so one graded failure cannot redden every later gate run; every file present there in the morning is a typed blocker the operator reviews first; (c) results/receipts/failed/context.json — if present, the honest full-context decode ratio undershot the 0.9 bound (12 full-attention layers walking 256K KV; the community precedent shows about a 2x falloff by 50-73k) — a typed performance finding routed to the optimization menu, deliberately NOT a campaign failure. Also render: the open-items list (every UNKNOWN from the spec with its drain state); the promotion checklist (what the operator verifies before any fleet change, per ruling P13 — and state the causality plainly: the fleet's local-models sync retires any staged artifact that has no catalog row; it pruned the staged checkpoint from BOTH nodes on 08-29 around 20:07/20:14; applying handoff/catalog-row.patch is the act that makes staging durable, and it must precede any rebuild or any restart of the model-sync trigger service); the transport-rung caveat (if any receipt records fn_transport_rung wire-fallback, the night ran on the 5GbE wire: valid but degraded receipts, and bench.json then does NOT satisfy the rail-sockets Gate 0 for verbs bring-up — healing rail 0 is the morning's first transport act); the optimization menu; and a blocker template implementing ruling P16. The optimization menu carries, beyond the original items (tuned mixture-kernel config generation for this GPU, graph-capture matrix, jumbo-frame A-B, draft-length sweep, the four-bit expert lane pointers from IMPORTS.md): the speculative-head depth sweep n in 1 to 4 plus the index-share and padded-drafter knobs (UNKNOWN-5); the attended RDMA go/no-go with the honest cost (2-4 attended hours, two more reboots, worker deploy-path fix first, nothing staged for kernel 7.2.2 yet) and honest expectation (about +3.4 percent measured precedent over held TCP); the stream-primitive morning decision rule (attended port of the reference doorbell allreduce onto the in-tree stream device ONLY if the banked exchange p50 at 8-16 KiB is at or under about 40 microseconds AND the bench matrix shows decode is allreduce-dominated — noting the stream bench likely runs attended in the morning after teardown, since it skips while the pair serves); the full-context decode probe follow-up when deferred; a rejected-with-reason register so nothing is re-litigated (the community int4-WMMA expert lane: bound to a different runtime's artifact, single-device only, unreachable even in its own public release; the indexer rotation plus FP4 QAT art: fidelity art for a different model family's trained indexer graph — our engine's indexer is weight-free bf16 with no such trained graph, so transplanting it would corrupt top-k selection); the load-phase page-cache drop-behind remedy pointer for repo issue 2 (release file pages in chunks behind the loader); a per-shape kernel block-size tuning item for the 2560x640 and 640x2560 expert shapes (community precedent: a forced tile choice beat the auto-selector on exactly these shapes); and a note to audit the drafter hidden-state versus prefix-cache position sync before the speculative profile is declared production (a community v1.1 fix records the failure mode: cached target prefix reused while the drafter state timeline sits elsewhere breaks multi-turn — the operator files the repo issue). Also write docs/ANNOUNCE.md: a short community post draft describing the setup (two 128 GB unified-memory desktops, two fast rails, one control wire), what was built overnight, where the evidence lives, and where benchmarks land. Boundaries: touch only docs/MORNING.md, docs/ANNOUNCE.md, and docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md.\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:471:      \"id\": \"cp-proxy\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:473:      \"title\": \"Checkpoint: proxy checkpoint first light, single node\",\nsilent-factory-worklis