{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016Z4B94vbyqs2KCBDtCbYqU","type":"tool_result","content":"| File | 54129 vs 53896 | Nature |\n|---|---|---|\n| `amd/ple_layer.py` | +1 line | **Only** `# TODO: need double-check` inserted above the `NULL_BLOCK_ID` remap (53896 line 519 region → 54129 `amd/ple_layer.py:522`). [S] Zero functional change; zero mmap wiring. |\n| `amd/model.py` | −8/+0 mmap-unrelated | Drops `is_model_fused_shared_expert_compatible` import, the `self.is_fused_shared_expert_enabled` computation, and the `enabled=` kwarg to `maybe_fuse_shared_experts`. Upstream-main API drift. [S] |\n| `amd/mtp.py` | same drift | identical `is_fused_shared_expert` removals. [S] |\n| `nvidia/mtp.py` | same drift | identical. [S] |\n| `nvidia/model.py` | +14/−12 [M] | 12 of those are upstream drift (as above); the mmap wiring is `from vllm.config import VllmConfig, get_current_vllm_config` (`:12`), `from . import ple_mmap` (`:77`), and two 5-line `build_tables` blocks at `:812-817` and `:1011-1016`. [S] |\n| `nvidia/ple_layer.py` | +89/−62 [M] | The whole mmap wiring, plus **a removal that changes the env-off path** — see below. |\n\n### Newer: `#54129`, by base. Later: `#53896`, by head timestamp.\n`#54129`'s head is literally a merge of `upstream-main` into `ple-mmap-upstream`, and its non-PLE churn (fused-MoE oracle, quark OCP MX, flashinfer utils, kimi_k3) is that merge. `#53896` never had `ple_mmap.py` (`grep -c PLE_MMAP vllm-pr53896/vllm/envs.py` → `0`; `find vllm-pr53896 -name 'ple_mmap*' -o -name 'test_ple_mmap*' | wc -l` → `0`) [M]. So the mmap feature is strictly additive on top of #53896's model code, but the two branches have **already diverged on shared non-mmap files** and a merge will conflict on `amd/{model,mtp}.py`, `nvidia/{model,mtp}.py`, `vllm/config/compilation.py`, and `vllm/envs.py`.\n\n### Surprise: #54129 changed the **env-off** nvidia path\n`#53896` routed the ID hashing through its own split-out custom op:\n```python\n# 53896 nvidia/ple_layer.py (removed by 54129)\n# Keep num_reqs-dependent ID generation outside PIECEWISE CUDA graphs,\n# which dispatch only on the padded token count.\ntorch.ops.vllm.qwen4_exp_compute_ple_ngram_ids(input_ids, query_start_loc, ngram_context, ngram_ids, self.layer_name)\n```\n`#54129` **deletes** `qwen4_exp_compute_ple_ngram_ids`, its fake impl, and its `direct_register_custom_op` registration (−35 lines), renames `compute_ngram_ids` → `_hash_ngram_ids`, and in the env-off branch calls it **inline, traced**: `nvidia/ple_layer.py:447-448` `ngram_ids = self._hash_ngram_ids(...); return self.ngram_embedding(ngram_ids).flatten(-2)`. [S] The op name also disappears from `_attention_ops`: `#53896` `vllm/config/compilation.py:770` had `\"vllm::qwen4_exp_compute_ple_ngram_ids\"`; `#54129` `:771` has `\"vllm::qwen4_exp_ple_mmap_forward\"` in its place. [M — `grep -n qwen4_exp` on both]\nIt is gone tree-wide: `grep -rn 'compute_ple_ngram_ids\\|compute_ngram_ids' vllm/ tests/` → no output. [M]\n\nAlso changed in the shared hashing body: `packed = self.padded_buffer[:num_reqs, :num_tokens]` (53896) → `packed = self.padded_buffer[:num_reqs]` (54129, `nvidia/ple_layer.py:379`). [S]\n\nThis contradicts `ple_mmap.py:32-35`'s claim [CL] that \"With `VLLM_PLE_MMAP` unset, nothing in this module is ever invoked and the stock classes are untouched.\" Nothing in *ple_mmap.py* is invoked — true — but the stock nvidia PLE forward and its cudagraph-splitting behavior **did** change. Whether that regresses PIECEWISE dispatch (the removed comment's stated concern) is **UNDETERMINED** from source; settling it needs a compile run with `-cc.cudagraph_mode=PIECEWISE` and a check of graph-split boundaries, or the PR author's rationale.\n\n---\n\n## 6. The piecewise-cudagraph guard, and its AMD analogue\n\n`nvidia/ple_mmap.py:597-635`, `check_cudagraph_safety(compilation_config)` — three independent refusals, any one of which alone would miss a route into a capture [S]:\n\n1. `:614-621` — `if compilation_config.cudagraph_mode.has_full_cudagraphs(): raise RuntimeError(...)`. Message: *\"VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 requires piecewise-only CUDA graphs … Pass `-cc.cudagraph_mode=PIECEWISE`.\"*\n2. `:622-628` — `if compilation_config.mode != CompilationMode.VLLM_COMPILE: raise` — *\"enforce-eager does not fully suppress CUDA graph capture on this model.\"*\n3. `:629-635` — `if QUALIFIED_OP_NAME not in (compilation_config.splitting_ops or []): raise` — guards against an operator-supplied `-cc.splitting_ops` or an attn-fusion reset silently dropping the op.\n\nCall site: `nvidia/ple_layer.py:284`, inside `Qwen4ExpNGramEmbedding.__init__`, i.e. at **construction time, before the ~78 GiB backbone streams** (`ple_mmap.py:703-704` comment [CL]). Tests pin all three: `tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_ple_mmap.py:661`, `:680`, `:691`, `:705`, plus construction-level mirrors at `:758`, `:786`, `:814`. [S]\n\n**What is the AMD analogue supposed to be? The same function, unchanged.** [S] The guard reads nothing platform-specific: `has_full_cudagraphs()` is `self.max_cudagraph_mode() == CUDAGraphMode.FULL` (`vllm/config/compilation.py:83-84`), `CompilationMode.VLLM_COMPILE` and `splitting_ops` are plain config. ROCm drives the identical `CUDAGraphMode` enum (`vllm/platforms/rocm.py:898-919`) and the identical `CUDAGraphWrapper` (`rocm.py:1002`). No HIP-graph-specific analogue is needed or exists.\n\nThe third check is **already satisfied on ROCm by default**: `\"vllm::qwen4_exp_ple_mmap_forward\"` sits unconditionally in the class-level `_attention_ops` (`vllm/config/compilation.py:764-782`, entry at `:771`), and `set_splitting_ops_for_v1` copies that list wholesale when `splitting_ops is None` (`vllm/config/compilation.py:1152-1161`, `self.splitting_ops = list(self._attention_ops)`). [S] The op *name* is in the default split set on every platform; only the op *implementation* is nvidia-gated.\n\n**AMD-specific tension worth flagging**: the AMD PLE short-conv path is written for FULL cudagraphs — `amd/ple_layer.py:522-525` [S]:\n```\n# TODO: need double-check\n# FULL cudagraph padded decode rows use NULL_BLOCK_ID. Remap them to\n# slot 0 for a safe gather, then zero output and skip write-back.\nvalid_state = state_indices != NULL_BLOCK_ID\n```\n(also `:642`, `:748`). Enabling `VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1` on AMD would force `cudagraph_mode=PIECEWISE` via check #1, taking the AMD tree off the mode its short-conv code was tuned for. That is a **performance/coverage decision the port must make explicitly**, not an incidental detail.\n\nAlso note: AMD's *existing* gather op, `vllm::qwen4_exp_amd_ple_ngram_embedding` (registered at `amd/ple_layer.py:1236-1241`, defined `:1217-1232`), is **not** in `_attention_ops` — `grep -n qwen4_exp vllm/config/compilation.py` returns only lines 770/771/772, none of which is the AMD op. [M] So today's AMD gather is opaque to Inductor but still *inside* the capture region. The port must not reuse it.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Every env var the PR introduces\n\nFour, all in `vllm/envs.py`. Type stubs at `:325-328`, lambdas at `:2168-2177`. [S]\n\n| Var | Default | Parse | Effect | Pins |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `VLLM_PLE_MMAP` | `False` (`\"0\"`) | `bool(int(os.getenv(...)))` | Master gate. `ple_mmap.enabled()` (`ple_mmap.py:116-118`) returns it; drives the constructor swap (`nvidia/ple_layer.py:282`), the three guards, the `load_weights` interception, and `build_tables` (`nvidia/model.py:813`, `:1012`). | `envs.py:325`, `:2170` |\n| `VLLM_PLE_MMAP_WORKERS` | `32` | `int(os.getenv(...))` | `ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=...)` for the gather pool; clamped `max(1, int(workers))`. Page faults overlap across threads. | `envs.py:326`, `:2172`; consumed `ple_mmap.py:906`; used `:327/:335` |\n| `VLLM_PLE_MMAP_CHUNK` | `2048` | `int(os.getenv(...))` | Rows per gather task; clamped `max(1, int(chunk))`. | `envs.py:327`, `:2174`; consumed `ple_mmap.py:907`; used `:325/:377` |\n| `VLLM_PLE_MMAP_PREWARM` | `False` (`\"0\"`) | `bool(int(os.getenv(...)))` | Streams the table once at load to warm page cache, bounded by `min(table_bytes, max(0, MemAvailable − 8 GiB))`. | `envs.py:328`, `:2177`; consumed `ple_mmap.py:913-921`; bound `:493-500` |\n\n**Compile-hash semantics** — `vllm/envs.py:2342-2350` adds the three *tuning* knobs to the ignored-factors set, deliberately leaving `VLLM_PLE_MMAP` itself a compile factor [S]:\n```\n# PLE mmap gather-pool tuning: affects only the CPU body of a\n# split-out op, never the compiled graph. VLLM_PLE_MMAP itself stays\n# a factor since it changes which op the graph splits around.\n\"VLLM_PLE_MMAP_WORKERS\", \"VLLM_PLE_MMAP_CHUNK\", \"VLLM_PLE_MMAP_PREWARM\",\n```\nConfirmed the PR adds no other env var: `grep -n '^+.*os\\.getenv\\|^+.*envs\\.VLLM_' pr54129.diff | grep -v PLE_MMAP` returns only pre-existing `VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT` reads and one `CompilationMode.VLLM_COMPILE` false positive. [M]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb415eb5-f590-4f10-83d3-19de6f536a77","uuid":"48da3ad5-24d0-4e2d-a06e-d106b0f966a9","timestamp":"2026-08-30T06:32:34.958Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"| File | 54129 vs 53896 | Nature |\n|---|---|---|\n| `amd/ple_layer.py` | +1 line | **Only** `# TODO: need double-check` inserted above the `NULL_BLOCK_ID` remap (53896 line 519 region → 54129 `amd/ple_layer.py:522`). [S] Zero functional change; zero mmap wiring. |\n| `amd/model.py` | −8/+0 mmap-unrelated | Drops `is_model_fused_shared_expert_compatible` import, the `self.is_fused_shared_expert_enabled` computation, and the `enabled=` kwarg to `maybe_fuse_shared_experts`. Upstream-main API drift. [S] |\n| `amd/mtp.py` | same drift | identical `is_fused_shared_expert` removals. [S] |\n| `nvidia/mtp.py` | same drift | identical. [S] |\n| `nvidia/model.py` | +14/−12 [M] | 12 of those are upstream drift (as above); the mmap wiring is `from vllm.config import VllmConfig, get_current_vllm_config` (`:12`), `from . import ple_mmap` (`:77`), and two 5-line `build_tables` blocks at `:812-817` and `:1011-1016`. [S] |\n| `nvidia/ple_layer.py` | +89/−62 [M] | The whole mmap wiring, plus **a removal that changes the env-off path** — see below. |\n\n### Newer: `#54129`, by base. Later: `#53896`, by head timestamp.\n`#54129`'s head is literally a merge of `upstream-main` into `ple-mmap-upstream`, and its non-PLE churn (fused-MoE oracle, quark OCP MX, flashinfer utils, kimi_k3) is that merge. `#53896` never had `ple_mmap.py` (`grep -c PLE_MMAP vllm-pr53896/vllm/envs.py` → `0`; `find vllm-pr53896 -name 'ple_mmap*' -o -name 'test_ple_mmap*' | wc -l` → `0`) [M]. So the mmap feature is strictly additive on top of #53896's model code, but the two branches have **already diverged on shared non-mmap files** and a merge will conflict on `amd/{model,mtp}.py`, `nvidia/{model,mtp}.py`, `vllm/config/compilation.py`, and `vllm/envs.py`.\n\n### Surprise: #54129 changed the **env-off** nvidia path\n`#53896` routed the ID hashing through its own split-out custom op:\n```python\n# 53896 nvidia/ple_layer.py (removed by 54129)\n# Keep num_reqs-dependent ID generation outside PIECEWISE CUDA graphs,\n# which dispatch only on the padded token count.\ntorch.ops.vllm.qwen4_exp_compute_ple_ngram_ids(input_ids, query_start_loc, ngram_context, ngram_ids, self.layer_name)\n```\n`#54129` **deletes** `qwen4_exp_compute_ple_ngram_ids`, its fake impl, and its `direct_register_custom_op` registration (−35 lines), renames `compute_ngram_ids` → `_hash_ngram_ids`, and in the env-off branch calls it **inline, traced**: `nvidia/ple_layer.py:447-448` `ngram_ids = self._hash_ngram_ids(...); return self.ngram_embedding(ngram_ids).flatten(-2)`. [S] The op name also disappears from `_attention_ops`: `#53896` `vllm/config/compilation.py:770` had `\"vllm::qwen4_exp_compute_ple_ngram_ids\"`; `#54129` `:771` has `\"vllm::qwen4_exp_ple_mmap_forward\"` in its place. [M — `grep -n qwen4_exp` on both]\nIt is gone tree-wide: `grep -rn 'compute_ple_ngram_ids\\|compute_ngram_ids' vllm/ tests/` → no output. [M]\n\nAlso changed in the shared hashing body: `packed = self.padded_buffer[:num_reqs, :num_tokens]` (53896) → `packed = self.padded_buffer[:num_reqs]` (54129, `nvidia/ple_layer.py:379`). [S]\n\nThis contradicts `ple_mmap.py:32-35`'s claim [CL] that \"With `VLLM_PLE_MMAP` unset, nothing in this module is ever invoked and the stock classes are untouched.\" Nothing in *ple_mmap.py* is invoked — true — but the stock nvidia PLE forward and its cudagraph-splitting behavior **did** change. Whether that regresses PIECEWISE dispatch (the removed comment's stated concern) is **UNDETERMINED** from source; settling it needs a compile run with `-cc.cudagraph_mode=PIECEWISE` and a check of graph-split boundaries, or the PR author's rationale.\n\n---\n\n## 6. The piecewise-cudagraph guard, and its AMD analogue\n\n`nvidia/ple_mmap.py:597-635`, `check_cudagraph_safety(compilation_config)` — three independent refusals, any one of which alone would miss a route into a capture [S]:\n\n1. `:614-621` — `if compilation_config.cudagraph_mode.has_full_cudagraphs(): raise RuntimeError(...)`. Message: *\"VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 requires piecewise-only CUDA graphs … Pass `-cc.cudagraph_mode=PIECEWISE`.\"*\n2. `:622-628` — `if compilation_config.mode != CompilationMode.VLLM_COMPILE: raise` — *\"enforce-eager does not fully suppress CUDA graph capture on this model.\"*\n3. `:629-635` — `if QUALIFIED_OP_NAME not in (compilation_config.splitting_ops or []): raise` — guards against an operator-supplied `-cc.splitting_ops` or an attn-fusion reset silently dropping the op.\n\nCall site: `nvidia/ple_layer.py:284`, inside `Qwen4ExpNGramEmbedding.__init__`, i.e. at **construction time, before the ~78 GiB backbone streams** (`ple_mmap.py:703-704` comment [CL]). Tests pin all three: `tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_ple_mmap.py:661`, `:680`, `:691`, `:705`, plus construction-level mirrors at `:758`, `:786`, `:814`. [S]\n\n**What is the AMD analogue supposed to be? The same function, unchanged.** [S] The guard reads nothing platform-specific: `has_full_cudagraphs()` is `self.max_cudagraph_mode() == CUDAGraphMode.FULL` (`vllm/config/compilation.py:83-84`), `CompilationMode.VLLM_COMPILE` and `splitting_ops` are plain config. ROCm drives the identical `CUDAGraphMode` enum (`vllm/platforms/rocm.py:898-919`) and the identical `CUDAGraphWrapper` (`rocm.py:1002`). No HIP-graph-specific analogue is needed or exists.\n\nThe third check is **already satisfied on ROCm by default**: `\"vllm::qwen4_exp_ple_mmap_forward\"` sits unconditionally in the class-level `_attention_ops` (`vllm/config/compilation.py:764-782`, entry at `:771`), and `set_splitting_ops_for_v1` copies that list wholesale when `splitting_ops is None` (`vllm/config/compilation.py:1152-1161`, `self.splitting_ops = list(self._attention_ops)`). [S] The op *name* is in the default split set on every platform; only the op *implementation* is nvidia-gated.\n\n**AMD-specific tension worth flagging**: the AMD PLE short-conv path is written for FULL cudagraphs — `amd/ple_layer.py:522-525` [S]:\n```\n# TODO: need double-check\n# FULL cudagraph padded decode rows use NULL_BLOCK_ID. Remap them to\n# slot 0 for a safe gather, then zero output and skip write-back.\nvalid_state = state_indices != NULL_BLOCK_ID\n```\n(also `:642`, `:748`). Enabling `VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1` on AMD would force `cudagraph_mode=PIECEWISE` via check #1, taking the AMD tree off the mode its short-conv code was tuned for. That is a **performance/coverage decision the port must make explicitly**, not an incidental detail.\n\nAlso note: AMD's *existing* gather op, `vllm::qwen4_exp_amd_ple_ngram_embedding` (registered at `amd/ple_layer.py:1236-1241`, defined `:1217-1232`), is **not** in `_attention_ops` — `grep -n qwen4_exp vllm/config/compilation.py` returns only lines 770/771/772, none of which is the AMD op. [M] So today's AMD gather is opaque to Inductor but still *inside* the capture region. The port must not reuse it.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Every env var the PR introduces\n\nFour, all in `vllm/envs.py`. Type stubs at `:325-328`, lambdas at `:2168-2177`. [S]\n\n| Var | Default | Parse | Effect | Pins |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `VLLM_PLE_MMAP` | `False` (`\"0\"`) | `bool(int(os.getenv(...)))` | Master gate. `ple_mmap.enabled()` (`ple_mmap.py:116-118`) returns it; drives the constructor swap (`nvidia/ple_layer.py:282`), the three guards, the `load_weights` interception, and `build_tables` (`nvidia/model.py:813`, `:1012`). | `envs.py:325`, `:2170` |\n| `VLLM_PLE_MMAP_WORKERS` | `32` | `int(os.getenv(...))` | `ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=...)` for the gather pool; clamped `max(1, int(workers))`. Page faults overlap across threads. | `envs.py:326`, `:2172`; consumed `ple_mmap.py:906`; used `:327/:335` |\n| `VLLM_PLE_MMAP_CHUNK` | `2048` | `int(os.getenv(...))` | Rows per gather task; clamped `max(1, int(chunk))`. | `envs.py:327`, `:2174`; consumed `ple_mmap.py:907`; used `:325/:377` |\n| `VLLM_PLE_MMAP_PREWARM` | `False` (`\"0\"`) | `bool(int(os.getenv(...)))` | Streams the table once at load to warm page cache, bounded by `min(table_bytes, max(0, MemAvailable − 8 GiB))`. | `envs.py:328`, `:2177`; consumed `ple_mmap.py:913-921`; bound `:493-500` |\n\n**Compile-hash semantics** — `vllm/envs.py:2342-2350` adds the three *tuning* knobs to the ignored-factors set, deliberately leaving `VLLM_PLE_MMAP` itself a compile factor [S]:\n```\n# PLE mmap gather-pool tuning: affects only the CPU body of a\n# split-out op, never the compiled graph. VLLM_PLE_MMAP itself stays\n# a factor since it changes which op the graph splits around.\n\"VLLM_PLE_MMAP_WORKERS\", \"VLLM_PLE_MMAP_CHUNK\", \"VLLM_PLE_MMAP_PREWARM\",\n```\nConfirmed the PR adds no other env var: `grep -n '^+.*os\\.getenv\\|^+.*envs\\.VLLM_' pr54129.diff | grep -v PLE_MMAP` returns only pre-existing `VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT` reads and one `CompilationMode.VLLM_COMPILE` false positive. [M]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
