{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeYUj1S8Mw6aNd45X2R59","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PPxtebnhMywFXWGec73U6E","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh tests/test_proxy_tooling.py && git status --porcelain && git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nproxy-tooling: Proxy checkpoint builder and single-node first-light runner\n\nscripts/make-proxy.sh builds the synthetic checkpoint at\n/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy inside flashnext:dev — the workload's own\n`architectures` identifier, four decoder layers (the smallest prefix that\ncarries both attention kinds at full_attention_interval 4), 8 routed experts\nin block-FP8 at weight_block_size 128x128, and a per-layer engram table\nwritten under the exact shard tensor name the fork's mmap path matches.\n\nThe generator invents nothing it can read instead:\n\n  * the tensor INVENTORY is derived from the staged workload checkpoint's\n    safetensors headers — header-only, zero weight bytes read, mounted\n    read-only — so the proxy is architecturally faithful without this lane\n    having to restate an architecture it cannot see;\n  * the shard tensor NAME is derived mechanically from the fork's own\n    `_SHARD_RE` and validated back through it, so the two cannot drift;\n  * the shard FILE convention is lifted from the fork's\n    tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_ple_mmap.py fixture;\n  * the row split reproduces the fork's `shard_size = ceil(org_vocab_size /\n    split_ngram_parts)` arithmetic verbatim;\n  * and the build ends by calling the fork's own discover_shards() on what\n    it wrote, so an undiscoverable table fails at build time, not at 3 a.m.\n\nA manifest records the shape signature and every file written; a rerun whose\nsignature matches and whose files are present skips the rebuild.\n\nscripts/run-proxy.sh serves that checkpoint single-node with VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1,\ntakes one greedy completion, asserts every returned per-token logprob finite\nthrough the API, stops the container and confirms it exited, and writes\nresults/receipts/proxy.json (fail receipts quarantined under\nresults/receipts/failed/ per D12). The receipt's data carries the serve env\nchoices and the full serve argv so cp-proxy and the TP=2 serve reproduce them\nrather than re-derive them, and a rerun that re-measures identical facts\nleaves the committed receipt byte-for-byte alone.\n\nIt pins the three serve facts from the 08-29 day run: the text-only\n--limit-mm-per-prompt that keeps the vision encoder's 274877906944-byte\nprofiling allocation out of the run (not the profiling-bypass flag, which\nonly defers that wall to the first real image); gpu_memory_utilization held\nat 0.6; and VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY left unset at any value, since these\nhosts log integrated_gpu=False and that steer was superseded.\n\nDEVIATION, deliberate and recorded: the lane asks for eager execution, but\nthe fork's check_cudagraph_safety refuses --enforce-eager while the mmap\ntable is armed (\"enforce-eager does not fully suppress CUDA graph capture on\nthis model\" — it requires CompilationMode.VLLM_COMPILE), and separately names\n-cc.cudagraph_mode=PIECEWISE as the remedy for full graphs. Graph-capture-free\nserving under the table is therefore spelled PIECEWISE, which is the mode the\nsuccessful proxy boot used and the mode host/fn-cluster-up.sh now serves TP=2\nin. FN_PROXY_EXEC_MODE=eager remains a real, working --enforce-eager branch\nfor a VLLM_PLE_MMAP=0 control run and refuses to arm itself beside the table\nrather than dying deep inside the engine. The chosen mode lands in the\nreceipt.\n\ntests/test_proxy_tooling.py (25 tests) extracts and imports the builder's\nembedded Python — written import-safe under a __main__ guard — and drives its\npure planning functions: the shard-name derivation round-tripped through the\nfork's real matcher, the row arithmetic, the inventory filter, the config\nrewrite. It also pins the serve doctrine, the eager refusal, the receipt\nshape, and that both scripts and every embedded Python body compile.\n\nExecuting run-proxy.sh is cp-proxy's; no receipt is committed here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\necho \"--- AC4 ---\"; bash -euc '[ -z \"$(git status --porcelain)\" ]'; echo \"AC4 rc=$?\"; git log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the lane and confirm it is clean"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":497,"cache_read_input_tokens":152455,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":497},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb415eb5-f590-4f10-83d3-19de6f536a77","uuid":"cf2d6927-d63e-43ed-9f7a-8a3e6a316c69","timestamp":"2026-08-30T06:43:18.355Z","request_id":"req_011CeYUizdWeAFWGTsAjVVb1"}
