{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeYUkim5rn6uey8kcHdox","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done — committed as `89a2844` on `tally-work/flashnext-62c1a4aeb3e6/proxy-tooling`, lane clean.\n\n## What landed\n\n**`scripts/make-proxy.sh`** — builds the synthetic checkpoint at `/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy` inside `flashnext:dev`, in `run-smoke.sh`'s shape (host half decides whether to run; everything effectful is one `podman run`). It refuses to invent what it can read:\n\n- Tensor **inventory** is derived from the staged workload checkpoint's safetensors *headers* — header-only, read-only mount, zero weight bytes read — so the proxy carries the workload's real architecture and `architectures` identifier without this lane restating a config it can't see.\n- The **shard tensor name** is derived mechanically from the fork's own `_SHARD_RE` and validated back through it (`shard_name_template` raises if the regex is no longer a plain two-index pattern).\n- The **shard file convention** is lifted out of `tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_ple_mmap.py`; the row split reproduces the fork's `shard_size = ceil(org_vocab_size / split_ngram_parts)` verbatim.\n- The build ends by calling the fork's `discover_shards()` on its own output — an undiscoverable table fails here, not at serve time.\n- Shape: 4 layers (smallest prefix carrying both attention kinds at `full_attention_interval 4`), 8 experts, `weight_block_size [128,128]`. A manifest records the signature + file list; a matching rerun skips the rebuild.\n\n**`scripts/run-proxy.sh`** — single-node serve with `VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1`, one greedy completion, every returned per-token logprob asserted finite via the API, container stopped and confirmed exited, receipt to `results/receipts/proxy.json` (fail twin quarantined under `failed/` per D12). `data` carries the serve env and full argv so cp-proxy and the TP=2 serve reproduce rather than re-derive them; a rerun measuring identical facts leaves the committed receipt byte-identical (overseer note 2).\n\n**`tests/test_proxy_tooling.py`** — 25 tests. Extracts the builder's embedded Python (written import-safe under a `__main__` guard) and drives the real planning functions; also pins the serve doctrine and receipt shape.\n\n## One deliberate deviation, flagged\n\nThe lane asks for **eager execution**, but the fork makes `--enforce-eager` illegal under `VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1`: `check_cudagraph_safety`'s second guard raises at construction with *\"enforce-eager does not fully suppress CUDA graph capture on this model\"* (it requires `CompilationMode.VLLM_COMPILE`), and its first guard names `-cc.cudagraph_mode=PIECEWISE` as the remedy. This is the repo's own hard-won record (`docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md` item 3; `host/fn-cluster-up.sh` already dropped the flag for the same reason). Serving `--enforce-eager` by default would have produced a script that cannot boot.\n\nSo graph-capture-free serving is spelled `PIECEWISE` by default — the mode the successful proxy boot used — and `FN_PROXY_EXEC_MODE=eager` is a real, working `--enforce-eager` branch for a `VLLM_PLE_MMAP=0` control that refuses to arm beside the table rather than dying inside the engine. Whichever branch runs is recorded in the receipt.\n\n## Verification\n\nAll four acceptance argv run and pass; full suite is 116/116; `git status --porcelain` empty. The scripts are authored and syntax-clean but **not executed** — no container, GPU, or staged workload on this box, and executing them is explicitly cp-proxy's job. No receipt is committed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1776,"cache_read_input_tokens":152952,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1776},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb415eb5-f590-4f10-83d3-19de6f536a77","uuid":"6ce4f181-a505-43f4-9e7d-4f9e1eb8cfe6","timestamp":"2026-08-30T06:43:38.753Z","request_id":"req_011CeYUkhj4wXJ2JJcLwZgUw"}
